  "id": "son_de_los_diablos",
  "name": "Son de los diablos (Afro-Peruvian carnival devils' dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The son de los diablos is the Afro-Peruvian carnival dance of Lima in which a troupe of masked devils led by a caporal parades through the streets with acrobatic zapateo footwork; a colonial-era festival custom painted by Pancho Fierro in the nineteenth century, it faded in the early twentieth and was revived on stage by Afro-Peruvian folklore companies from the mid-century. Its music is carried by guitar, cajón and the quijada, the rattled jawbone of a donkey.",
